A||||13||BAM-BAM||HP Question> What if I......?||||6||
Z||000000||BAM-BAM||04-19-2001||07:49 PM|||| I just bought a brand new 3.4L crate engine from GM. It is supposed to have about 166bhp. Is this correct? Now what kind of power gain would I get if I put on headers, a free flow cat and my Borla catback? I was told just that with headers and all the others I described, that I could expect an additional 25-30hp. is that correct. What other ignitin type mods can I make to increase HP? I will be getting an underdrive pully (I know, not much) and working on a ram air type setup. I am just a little leary about tearing down a new engine and doing a bunch of machine work. LMK and TIA<P>Peace, B2 OUT!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Knowledge is POWER!<BR>That is why the ignorant remain Weak!||||reg||6
Z||000001||88formula||04-19-2001||08:34 PM||||WOW you bought a new crate 3.4-liter engine from GM. The 166 horsepower figure came from me. You must have read some of my posts in the past. I used Dyno2000 to come up with those figures. <P>Here’s the deal, if you just bolt the motor just the way it is into you fiero with the stock manifolds and exhaust system you will have 160 horsepower @ 5000 rpm and 200 ft- lbs. of torque @ 3500 rpm. <P>If you use your Borla exhaust system and ported or sprint exhaust manifolds you should have around 170 horsepower @ 5000 rpm and 208 ft. lbs. of torque @ 3500 rpm. <P>If you Install real headers like the FOCOA headers with the Borla exhaust system than you should have around 190 horsepower @ 5000 rpm and 222 ft. lbs. of torque @ 4000 rpm. So that is a 30 horsepower gain over the stock setup.<P>I don't know if you have an automatic or a manual transmission so I'll guess and say you have the five-speed manual. With the FOCOA headers, Borla exhaust system, and free flowing cat your fiero should go 0-60 mph in 6 seconds and run the quarter mile in 14.2 seconds @ 95 mph.  This is if you launch @ 2500 rpm with little or no tire spin at an elevation of 800 ft. and a temperature of 75 degrees.  <P>Keep in mind that this program assumes you have the perfect air fuel ratios and spark advance with no detonation when calculating your power output. You may need to get a custom prom chip made to get those perfect air fuel ratios and spark curves.<P>A good multi spark ignition system would give you around 1-3 horsepower gain depending on the condition of your old ignition system. 1FST2M6 could help you with the ignition stuff because he has a lot of experience with that stuff.  <P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88formula_logo_1.JPG">    <P><p>[This message has been edited by 88formula (edited 04-19-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||Old Lar||04-19-2001||08:42 PM||||Well if a stock 3.8L makes 200-220 hp, a 3.8 s/c makes 240 hp, with some tweeking you should get out 200-210 hp from the 3.4L.  The 3.8 is 231 cubic inches, the 3.4 has 207 cubic inches.  The old days 1 hp/cubic inch was always doable.||||reg||3
Z||000003||88formula||04-19-2001||09:03 PM||||It's really 204.4 cubic inches. ||||reg||1
Z||000004||Dave Gunsul||04-19-2001||10:02 PM||||I agree with Formula88 about the MSD box.<BR>I have one and it helps.<BR>My suggestion would be to add a bored out t-body with matching plenum and possibly gasket<BR>matching the lower intake. The Fieor's intake<BR>system is fine for the 2.8 but when you start adding cubes the T-body especially becomes the weak link.||||reg||1
Z||000005||BAM-BAM||04-20-2001||08:14 AM|||| I'll reply later, have to go to work now. But I have some interesting notes to add to all that. I've heared the the T-Body just heps you realize the same throttle perametera at a lower throttle position. I'll be back!<P>Thankd guys!! B2 OUT!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Knowledge is POWER!<BR>That is why the ignorant remain Weak!||||reg||12
