Z||000012||BAM-BAM||04-20-2001||11:57 PM||||  Ok, 88 and 1Fst, I am running an automatic first off, so I guess those performance numbers may be a little off. I am planning on porting and polishing the heads, port matching the intake and whatever manifold or header I use. I was thinking about a bored out TB but was informed that the real response is just quicker peddle reaction. However it does make some sense that more air and fuel means more power. I am also in the process of obtaining 19# injectors from a late modle Mustang 5.0, is this the correct way to go? I was also informed that if my fuel pump had good rail pressure (@40#) that a larger fuel pump and regulator were unneccessary. I want to get the hard mods on before the engine goes into the car, ie..headers, under drive pulley. I will be running CW's Ultimate cat and my Borla. The headers are the question. Where can I get me hands on some info on FOCOA headers? I cant seem to find pricing anywhere. I will be running a custom PROM. I would ultimately like to see 205-210 HP without any head work ( if possible). That way when and if I get the heads worked, I should be near 230-235? Of course at that time I will look for a moderate performance cam also. As for ignition, MSD is the preference? Has anyone used the Crane PS91 coil? what other ignition mods will help my power gains? I know, so many questions. Well I need to be informed if I am going to make the proper decisions. Let me know what your thoughts and opinions are.  TIA<P>Peace, B2 OUT!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Knowledge is POWER!<BR>That is why the ignorant remain Weak!||||reg||12
